Hi, Eric.  I see that Ken has already told you how to get water.  If
only there were some natural way to figure these things out while
playing.  I agree that #fill makes more sense than #dip.  Another way
to get rid of your dagger is to force some more chests with it.  Maybe
it will break.  It's kind of nice of nethack not to leave you wielding
a cursed -3 stump of a broken dagger.  Too nice if you ask me.
Wielding a cursed weapon is one of the worst things that can happen to
you in the early stages of play.  Perhaps you can suggest an
improvement to the interface that would make it less likely that you
wield the wrong thing.  I think that an option to require confirmation
on *all* wields via wx would be OK.  This would help out, too, when
you accidentally try to wield your newt corpse or your potion of
paralysis.  If you type w*x or w?x then confirmation would not be
needed since that form of the command displays your list first.
Whenever I am not on a slow system I prefer the w*x form.  I don't think
that my suggestion would give anything away, and of course no one would
be forced to use it.


